<title>EGYPT: Egypt raises benchmark crude price 40 cts for July.</title>
<headline>Egypt raises benchmark crude price 40 cts for July.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Egyptian General Petroleum Corp (EGPC) has raised by 40 cents the price of its benchmark Gulf of Suez blend against Dated Brent for July, an EGPC official told Reuters on Thursday.</p>
<p>The official said EGPC had also raised prices by 10 to 20 cents on five other crudes. Following are details of July crude prices, all against Dated Brent (June differentials in brackets):</p>
<p>    Gulf of Suez	-$2.10 (-$2.50)</p>
<p>    Belayim	     -$3.55 (-$3.65)</p>
<p>    Ras Gharib	  -$4.05 (-$4.25)</p>
<p>    Ras Badran	  -$3.50 (-$3.70)</p>
<p>    Ras el-Behar	-$1.95 (-$2.05)</p>
<p>    Zeit Bay	    -$2.00 (-$2.10)</p>
<p>-- Esmat Salaheddin +202 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
